        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "a0505283-6010-5165-8111-ac2496d6addf",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport, Rickenbacker International Airport, Carolina, Puerto Rico, San Juan, Puerto Rico, Lockbourne, Ohio, Franklin County, Ohio, Columbus, Ohio\n- Organizations: Pro-Air Services\n- Concepts: civil-military airports, airport codes, airport naming\n\nFacts:\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is a joint civil-military international airport in suburban Carolina, Puerto Rico, 3 miles southeast of San Juan.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport uses the codes IATA SJU, ICAO TJSJ, and FAA LID SJU.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is also known as Isla Verde International Airport or Aeropuerto Internacional de Isla Verde.\n- Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport is named for Puerto Rico's first democratically elected governor.\n- Pro-Air Services is an air charter operator based at Luis Muñoz Marín International Airport in San Juan, Puerto Rico.\n- Rickenbacker International Airport is a civil-military public airport near Lockbourne in southern Franklin County, Ohio, 10 miles south of downtown Columbus.\n- Rickenbacker International Airport uses the codes IATA LCK, ICAO KLCK, and FAA LID LCK.\n- Lockbourne is located near Rickenbacker International Airport.\n- Lockbourne originally gave Rickenbacker International Airport its former name, Lockbourne Air Force Base.",
